# The build-context ignore for EVERY image: all five are `--target`s of the root Dockerfile and
# share this one context. It is also the only ignore file that the LEGACY docker builder honours
# (per-Dockerfile ignore files are BuildKit-only; a legacy build silently skipped them and
# `COPY . /app` then baked secrets + the answer key into the image, #137). Isolation here is
# therefore builder- and target-independent. tests/test_sandbox_image_purity.py pins the entries.
.git
.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
spikes
spec/references
# Secrets — must never enter any image (#137, trusted-submitter creds never reach a worker).
.env
# Isolation (#137): the agent runs inside the sandbox image — no datasets (the ablation answer key
# lives under data/*/verifier/), no prior run results, no analysis figures.
data
results
figures
